        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Daburiyya, Nazareth, Israel's Northern District, Israel\n- Topics: names and transliterations, location, population demographics\n\nFacts:\n- Daburiyya is an Arab village about 8 km east of Nazareth in Israel's Northern District.\n- Daburiyya is also spelled Deburieh or Dabburieh, and its name is given in Arabic and Hebrew.\n- Nazareth is the capital and largest city in the Northern District of Israel.\n- Nazareth is also named in Hebrew, Arabic, and Aramaic transliterations.\n- The inhabitants of Nazareth are predominantly Arab citizens of Israel.\n- In Nazareth, 69% of the inhabitants are Muslim and 30.9% are Christian.",
